      "writtenOn": "2025-08-22T09:35:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see that we have added a new generic `FinalizeMapImpl` function to replace the backend implementation details\u0027 version below. But it\u0027s unimplemented for now. Could we add a TODO here to make it less confusing why we have two \"FinalizeMap\" functions.\n\nNevertheless, I think the generic function could be difficult to replace the function below. The current version depends on `ScopedCommandRecordingContext` which contains a scoped lock. Our current implementation locks the context once then calls `FinalizeMap` on multiple buffers.\n```\n  ScopedCommandRecordingContext context(...);\n  for (pendingBuffers) {\n  \tFinalizeMap(\u0026context, pendingBuffers);\n  }\n```\n\nIf we wanted to use the generic `FinalizeMapImpl` in future, we could have to lock the context repeatedly for each buffer. That would increase the overhead.",
